=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The network is fully healthy and the ticket describes a fault that does not exist
in the current lab state. Direct measurement disproves every element of the
complaint:

- Connectivity: a live ping from pc_0_0 (10.0.0.2) to pc_0_1 (10.0.1.2)
  returned 4/4 packets with 0% loss and sub-2 ms RTT.

- Uplinks on leaf_router_0_1: both eth0 (172.16.0.7/31, toward
  spine_router_0_0:eth2) and eth1 (172.16.0.11/31, toward
  spine_router_0_1:eth2) show kernel state UP/LOWER_UP — the physical carrier
  is present on both links.

- BGP control plane: leaf_router_0_1 has two fully Established eBGP sessions,
  one to each spine (172.16.0.6 / AS 65100 and 172.16.0.10 / AS 65101), each
  with uptime ~2m30s, 1 prefix received and 2 prefixes advertised. The route
  to 10.0.0.0/24 is installed in leaf_router_0_1's FIB via eth0, and
  10.0.1.0/24 is installed in leaf_router_0_0's FIB via its eth0.

- The spine-side link endpoints (spine_router_0_0:eth2 and
  spine_router_0_1:eth2) are also UP with correct /31 addresses.

Root cause: there is no fault. The ticket is a false alarm — the reporter's
premise that both uplinks of leaf_router_0_1 are down is incorrect. No
corrective action is needed; the fabric is operating normally end-to-end.
=== END ===
